      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/773840/000077384026000143/hon-20260930.htm",
      "excerpt": "In addition to growing in our core end-markets, we are concentrating on additional expansion in four “high-growth vertical” areas: data centers, semiconductors, life sciences, and LNG, where we bring our portfolio together around customer outcomes that matter most. In each vertical, we aim to build scale through vertical-specific offerings, a tailored commercial approach, and targeted acquisitions and partnerships. By way of example, in data centers, we help operators maximize uptime and energy efficiency by integrating building management, power and cooling controls, fire safety, and security. In our semiconductor vertical we help fabrication facilities protect yield and operate safely through environmental controls, gas detection, and process automation. And in LNG, we help producers improve throughput, reliability, and safety across liquefaction and export operations through process control, safety systems, and operations software. For example, for pharmaceutical and biotechnology manufacturers, one of our core focuses is on improving manufacturing quality: small deviations in temperature, humidity, pressure, or contamination control can compromise a batch and create regulatory exposure. We address this by integrating our process automation software and controls, building management systems, and fire and security solutions into a seamless solution for our customers. Building controls hold the precise environmental conditions production requires; process automation provides real-time visibility into production data across the manufacturing lifecycle; and fire and security systems protect people, facilities, and product while supporting compliance with stringent regulations. Together, these capabilities help customers improve product quality, simplify regulatory compliance, and lower operating costs. Because our capabilities apply across verticals, lessons from one domain carry into others, which we believe deepens our relationships with existing customers. Capitalize on our extensive global footprint as an automation leader As a pure-play automation company, we have global scale with over half of our total annual sales from outside of the United States, and approximately one-third of total annual sales from high-growth regions. As reshoring investments remain strong, we believe this global mix positions us well to meet the local needs of customers for longevity of human life, energy demand / security, and increased energy consumption. Our global scale and reach are bolstered by the strength of our trusted brand and the depth of our channel partnerships.",
